  "passage": "The classroom fan made a clicking sound every time it turned. Students found it annoying during quiet reading.\nThe school could not replace it immediately, so the class tried to solve the problem. They moved one loose wire away from the blades and cleaned dust from the cover. The clicking became softer but did not disappear.\nDuring reading time, the teacher played quiet background music. The clicking was less noticeable.\nA new fan arrived two weeks later. Everyone was happy, but the teacher praised the class for trying.\nThey had not fully fixed the problem, but they had made it better.\nNot every problem can be solved at once. Sometimes improvement is still worth doing.",
